OPTIONAL follow-up, not pushed anywhere.

PR #53 (Django 6) passes CI without this, so it was deliberately left off the
Renovate branch (Renovate owns renovate/django-6.x and force-pushes over it
when it rebases). Apply it on main after #53 merges if you want the package
metadata to stop advertising Python 3.9 support, which Django 6 does not
provide: Django 6 declares "Requires-Python >=3.12".

For the same reason the readme "Requirements" line ("Python 3.10+ (3.15
recommended, used by CI and Docker)") is now inaccurate; that line is not
covered by this patch.

From 2ac6763009e221ae7afc1bae70f952640bfad7db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cline <cline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 03:35:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] chore: require Python >=3.12 for Django 6 and re-run CI

Django 6 declares 'Requires-Python >=3.12', but this project advertised
requires-python '>=3.9' and its CI and Docker image were pinned to Python
3.11, so installing the upgrade failed with:

    ERROR: Ignored the following versions that require a different python version: 6.1.2 Requires-Python >=3.12
    ERROR: Could not find a version that satisfies the requirement Django==6.1.2

The Python 3.15 bump has since landed on main (PR #43), so CI and the image now
satisfy Django's floor. Align the package metadata with it here and re-run the
checks against the new base.
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index b9aa526..2dc10cd 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ build-backend = "setuptools.build_meta"
 name = "pol"
 version = "0.0.2"
 description = "RSS generator website"
-requires-python = ">=3.9"
+requires-python = ">=3.12" # Django 6 declares Requires-Python >=3.12
 
 [tool.semantic_release]
 version_toml = ["pyproject.toml:project.version"]
-- 
